    content: `<p><b>Periodic Performance Evaluation</b><br>As an intern or employee of AUXOSYS ("the Company"), your work performance, conduct, and overall contribution will be subject to regular and systematic evaluation by your immediate supervisors and the Human Resources department. This evaluation process is designed to ensure alignment with the Company's standards, objectives, and operational expectations. The evaluation will include, but is not limited to, the following criteria:<ul><li><b>Quality and Timeliness of Deliverables:</b> Assessment of your ability to meet project requirements, adhere to deadlines, and produce work that meets the Company's quality standards.</li><li><b>Professionalism and Conduct:</b> Evaluation of your adherence to Company policies, including respect for colleagues, communication skills, and ethical behaviour.</li><li><b>Attendance and Punctuality:</b> Monitoring of your presence during scheduled working hours, timely reporting, and compliance with leave policies.</li><li><b>Collaboration and Initiative:</b> Your willingness to work collaboratively within teams, contribute ideas, and demonstrate proactivity in fulfilling your role.</li><li><b>Compliance with Company Protocols:</b> Strict adherence to all operational, security, confidentiality, and safety guidelines as stipulated by the Company.</li></ul></p><p><b>Performance Improvement and Feedback</b><ul><li>Periodic feedback sessions will be conducted to provide you with insights into your strengths and areas requiring improvement.</li><li>In case of identified performance gaps, you may be placed on a Performance Improvement Plan (PIP) outlining specific goals, timelines, and support mechanisms to help you meet required standards.</li><li>Your progress during the PIP period will be closely monitored, and failure to demonstrate sufficient improvement may lead to further action.</li></ul></p><p><b>Grounds for Termination</b><br>Your services may be terminated immediately and without prior notice under any of the following circumstances:<ul><li><b>Unsatisfactory Performance:</b> Failure to meet the minimum performance standards as determined through the Company's internal evaluation process, including non-compliance with deadlines, poor quality of work, or failure to improve after being placed on a PIP.</li><li><b>Breach of Company Policies:</b> Any violation of Company protocols, including but not limited to confidentiality breaches, misconduct, insubordination, harassment, misuse of Company assets, or failure to comply with instructions.</li><li><b>Gross Misconduct:</b> Any act or behaviour deemed grossly inappropriate or damaging to the Company's reputation, operations, or work environment.</li><li><b>Absence Without Authorisation:</b> Failure to attend work without a valid reason or approval from the Company, including unauthorised leave or absenteeism.</li></ul></p><p><b>Consequences of Termination</b><ul><li>In the event of termination under the grounds stated above, you will not be entitled to any further stipend, salary, bonuses, or benefits beyond the date of termination.</li><li>The Company reserves the right to withhold issuance of any completion certificates, experience letters, or reference letters if termination is due to unsatisfactory performance or policy breaches.</li><li>You will be required to complete all exit formalities, including returning Company property and clearing any pending obligations, prior to the termination becoming effective.</li></ul></p><p><b>Finality of Decision</b><br>The Company's decision regarding performance evaluations and termination will be final and binding. You acknowledge and accept that the Company retains sole discretion to terminate your engagement in accordance with the terms of this clause.</p>`,
