    content: `<p><b>Ownership of Intellectual Property</b><br>All intellectual property rights, including but not limited to inventions, discoveries, designs, processes, methods, technologies, software code, documents, data, reports, presentations, and any other work product developed, created, or contributed to by you, whether solely or jointly with others, during the course of your internship/employment with AUXOSYS ("the Company") shall be the exclusive property of the Company.</p><p>This includes, but is not limited to:<ul><li>Source code, software applications, algorithms, and technical documentation.</li><li>Research findings, experimental data, and prototypes.</li><li>Marketing materials, branding concepts, and business strategies.</li><li>Any written, visual, or digital materials produced for or on behalf of the Company.</li></ul></p><p><b>Assignment of Rights</b><br>You agree to:<ul><li>Provide all necessary assistance to the Company, including executing documents, cooperating in securing, maintaining, and enforcing intellectual property rights worldwide.</li><li>Disclose promptly to the Company any inventions or works created during your engagement that relate to the Company's business or anticipated business activities.</li></ul></p><p><b>Confidentiality and Non-Disclosure</b><br>All intellectual property and related information shall be treated as confidential and proprietary. You shall not disclose, reproduce, or use any of the Company's intellectual property for personal purposes or for the benefit of any third party without prior written authorisation from the Company.</p><p><b>Prohibition on Unauthorised Use</b><br>Any unauthorised use, replication, distribution, sale, publication, or modification of the Company's intellectual property by you, whether during or after your internship/employment, will be considered a serious breach of this agreement and the Company's policies.</p><p>Such a violation will expose you to:<ul><li>Immediate disciplinary action, including termination of your internship/employment.</li><li>Legal action for infringement of intellectual property rights under applicable laws, including the Indian Copyright Act, Patents Act, and Information Technology Act.</li><li>Claims for monetary damages, injunctive relief, and any other remedies available under law.</li></ul></p><p><b>Survival of Intellectual Property Obligations</b><br>Your obligations under this clause shall continue even after the termination or conclusion of your internship/employment with the Company, irrespective of the reason for termination.</p>`,
