    id: "post_termination",
    title: "Post-Termination Responsibilities (Annexure C)",
    content: `<p><b>Return of Company Assets</b><br>Upon the termination or conclusion of your internship/employment with AUXOSYS ("the Company"), whether voluntary or involuntary, you are required to immediately return all Company property in your possession, custody, or control. This includes, but is not limited to:<ul><li>Physical assets such as laptops, mobile devices, access cards, keys, hardware, and any other equipment issued to you.</li><li>All confidential documents, manuals, printed or digital materials, and any proprietary information in any form.</li><li>Any Company-owned software, data storage devices, backup media, or electronic files.</li></ul></p><p>Failure to return any Company assets in a timely and proper condition will be considered a serious breach and may result in the Company pursuing legal remedies to recover or compensate for such loss or damage.</p><p><b>Completion of Formal Handover</b><br>You are obligated to conduct a thorough handover of your duties, responsibilities, and ongoing projects before your departure. This includes but is not limited to:<ul><li>Submit all pending deliverables, project documentation, status reports, and knowledge transfer notes to your designated supervisor or team members.</li><li>Cooperating with the Company and your replacement (if applicable) to ensure a smooth transition and continuity of work.</li><li>Providing access credentials, passwords, and any other relevant information related to your role to authorised personnel.</li></ul></p><p>Non-compliance with the handover process may result in withholding of final stipend, certificates, or other exit formalities until satisfactory completion.</p><p><b>Non-Solicitation and Non-Contact Obligations</b><br>For a period of six (6) months following the termination or conclusion of your engagement, you shall be strictly prohibited from:<ul><li>Contacting, soliciting, or attempting to engage with any current clients, customers, vendors, partners, or affiliates of the Company, either directly or indirectly.</li><li>Using, sharing, or exploiting any confidential or proprietary knowledge, trade secrets, or intellectual property gained during your internship/employment for personal benefit or the benefit of any third party.</li><li>This non-solicitation and confidentiality obligation applies regardless of whether your termination was voluntary or involuntary.</li></ul></p><p><b>Legal Enforcement</b><br>Any breach of the post-termination responsibilities outlined above will be considered a violation of the terms of your internship/employment agreement and Company policies. The Company reserves the right to:<ul><li>Initiate appropriate civil and criminal legal action to protect its interests and enforce compliance.</li><li>Seek damages, injunctive relief, and any other remedies available under applicable laws, including but not limited to the Indian Contract Act, Information Technology Act, and laws governing trade secrets and confidentiality.</li></ul></p><p><b>Survival Clause</b><br>The obligations under this Post-Termination Responsibilities clause shall survive the termination of your internship/employment agreement and remain in full force and effect for the specified duration and as long as necessary to protect the Company's legitimate interests.</p>`,
